      "sourceTextSha256": "142d4f05a6870bacb1dbc19a36737f9a554aba833787b08967c226dc91adb0a6",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. At the agreed time, start the tour to Cocora Valley, appreciating the beautiful landscape of the area. Upon arrival at the Valley, enjoy a welcome cocktail (canelazo) and receive assistance from a specialized eco-guide who will introduce you to the Cocora Natural Reserve.\n\nWalking, transfer to the palm forest where you can appreciate the biodiversity of the local flora and fauna, and take the ecological trail of the tallest wax palm in the world, the national tree emblem. You will participate in the Quindío wax palm ritual, which involves learning about the history of how indigenous people revered this palm. Then, continue with the planting of palm seedlings.\n\nTransfer to the typical town of Salento, where you will have a walking tour visiting its colonial streets, artisan workshops, and the Cocora viewpoint. Return to the hotel. Accommodation.\n\nDuration: Approximately 7 hours\n\nIncludes: Professional Spanish-speaking tour guide with environmental interpretation, private transportation, wax palm ritual, and canelazo tasting.\n\nOptional Supplement: Lunch: 30 USD per person.",
